{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"The corrected buffer contract removed corruption, but a controlled all-one-scale case is still uncorrelated with either SwiGLU half ordering. That rules out scale layout and points to the assembly fused kernel expecting a different FP8/weight storage convention. I’m testing the lower-level row-major block-scale GEMM primitive next, which should reveal the compatible backend without another verification attempt."}}
